      {
        "quote": "Unclear, with multiple theories."
      },
      {
        "quote": "* From the story of the 油鉢 (yuhatsu, “pot of oil”) in the Mahāparinirvāṇa Sūtra (大般涅槃経); see 大般涅槃経#油断大敵."
      },
      {
        "quote": "*:"
      },
      {
        "quote": "* Sound change from 寛(ゆた)に (yuta ni)."
      },
      {
        "quote": "* There is a lamp in Enryaku-ji (延暦寺) that has been alight since the time of Saichō (最澄), its founder, and 油断 (literally “oil + end”) refers to not letting it go out."
